Third-party notices for chobo
=============================

chobo's table of the characters a name of chobo's may hold and a Rust name may not
(src/client/xid.rs, DESIGN.md 14), which E063 and the Rust clients read, is made from two files
of the Unicode Character Database:

  Unicode Character Database 17.0.0, https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/
    DerivedCoreProperties.txt        the properties Alphabetic, XID_Start and XID_Continue
    extracted/DerivedGeneralCategory.txt
                                     the general categories of the numbers (Nd, Nl and No)

tools/xid/make_table.py writes the table from the two files, and the head of the table gives
each file's date and SHA-256. The table is two lists of ranges of code points; chobo reads
nothing at run time. The files say that their terms of use and license are at
https://www.unicode.org/terms_of_use.html, which puts the Unicode data files under the Unicode
License v3, https://www.unicode.org/license.txt (SPDX-License-Identifier: Unicode-3.0). Its
